# The agent's context window has to be set on the SERVER, not the request.
#
# Deriving the model with the parameter baked in gives you two things: a stable short name
# (`agentgraph-mellum2-thinking`, which is what DEFAULT_MODEL in src/agentgraph/config.py expects)
# and a context window that is right however you reach the server. It is one command, identical
# on every platform.
#
#   ollama pull hf.co/JetBrains/Mellum2-12B-A2.5B-Thinking-GGUF-Q4_K_M
#   ollama create agentgraph-mellum2-thinking -f Modelfile
#
# This is the THINKING checkpoint, not the Instruct one the previous workshop used. Same
# weights, trained to emit reasoning inside <think>...</think> before it answers. Tool calling
# is native to it, so there is nothing extra to pull or enable — Ollama's chat template parses
# both the reasoning and the tool calls, and `ChatOllama` hands them back on separate channels.
# See src/agentgraph/llm/client.py.
#
# Verify with `ollama ps` after one request: the CONTEXT column must read 16384.
# `agentgraph doctor` checks this for you, along with the two things that are new in this
# edition — that the model actually reasons, and that it can still call a tool while doing it.

FROM hf.co/JetBrains/Mellum2-12B-A2.5B-Thinking-GGUF-Q4_K_M

PARAMETER num_ctx 16384
